WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.067
We are being told this morning

00:00:01.067 --> 00:00:01.534
that Trump's

00:00:01.534 --> 00:00:03.169
defense team is likely to attack

00:00:03.169 --> 00:00:04.738
the credibility of a major witness

00:00:04.738 --> 00:00:05.338
in the Manhattan

00:00:05.338 --> 00:00:06.706
district attorney's case.

00:00:06.706 --> 00:00:07.640
Michael Cohen,

00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:08.742
the former Trump lawyer,

00:00:08.742 --> 00:00:10.343
was convicted of lying to Congress,

00:00:10.343 --> 00:00:12.145
among other financial crimes.

00:00:12.145 --> 00:00:13.780
He says, are you pled guilty to that?

00:00:13.780 --> 00:00:14.614
We should note.

00:00:14.614 --> 00:00:16.282
He says he is proof this morning

00:00:16.282 --> 00:00:19.953
that he is telling the truth here

00:00:20.186 --> 00:00:21.454
I am a convicted felon

00:00:21.454 --> 00:00:23.556
and I am a disbarred lawyer, but

00:00:23.556 --> 00:00:26.192
I also brought the documents.

00:00:26.192 --> 00:00:27.894
There's plenty of testimony,

00:00:27.894 --> 00:00:30.130
corroborating testimony to go around.

00:00:30.130 --> 00:00:31.865
And at the end of the day,

00:00:31.865 --> 00:00:33.466
we have an indictment today.

00:00:33.466 --> 00:00:34.601
So clearly

00:00:34.601 --> 00:00:36.803
that means that the information provided

00:00:37.037 --> 00:00:39.072
was more than enough for the grand jury.

00:00:39.072 --> 00:00:39.773
To come back

00:00:39.773 --> 00:00:40.840
with the determination

00:00:40.840 --> 00:00:41.608
for an indictment or,

00:00:41.608 --> 00:00:42.175
by the way,

00:00:42.175 --> 00:00:42.876
for Donald,

00:00:42.876 --> 00:00:44.144
since we're talking about

00:00:44.144 --> 00:00:45.478
convicted felons.

00:00:45.478 --> 00:00:46.813
See, on Tuesday, pal. Hmm.

00:00:48.214 --> 00:00:50.083
Joining us now is Jim Trusty.

00:00:50.083 --> 00:00:51.985
He is a current attorney for Trump

00:00:51.985 --> 00:00:52.952
and the Department of Justice

00:00:52.952 --> 00:00:54.854
probe into the 2020 election,

00:00:54.854 --> 00:00:56.289
as well as the investigation

00:00:56.289 --> 00:00:58.058
involving classified documents

00:00:58.058 --> 00:00:58.858
at Mar a Lago

00:00:58.858 --> 00:00:59.592
Good morning, Jim,

00:00:59.592 --> 00:01:01.127
and thank you for being here.

00:01:01.127 --> 00:01:02.429
You're not representing Trump

00:01:02.429 --> 00:01:03.696
in this Manhattan case,

00:01:03.696 --> 00:01:04.564
we should make clear.

00:01:04.564 --> 00:01:05.832
But you are on his legal team.

00:01:05.832 --> 00:01:06.132
Obviously,

00:01:06.132 --> 00:01:07.434
you spent a lot of time with him.

00:01:07.434 --> 00:01:08.701
Do you expect that he's actually

00:01:08.701 --> 00:01:10.904
going to surrender himself on Tuesday,

00:01:10.904 --> 00:01:13.273
as we've been talking about

00:01:14.074 --> 00:01:15.341
Yeah, I don't have any inside

00:01:15.341 --> 00:01:16.576
info to share on that.

00:01:16.576 --> 00:01:17.844
I mean, we'll sort through it.

00:01:17.844 --> 00:01:19.079
We'll deal with the process.

00:01:19.079 --> 00:01:19.779
I think right now

00:01:19.779 --> 00:01:20.213
we're dealing

00:01:20.213 --> 00:01:22.449
with the enormity of the injustice

00:01:22.782 --> 00:01:24.617
and the shock of seeing people

00:01:24.617 --> 00:01:25.952
like Michael Cohen

00:01:25.952 --> 00:01:27.554
touted as credible witnesses.

00:01:27.554 --> 00:01:29.522
Or maybe he'll have Avenatti

00:01:29.522 --> 00:01:31.291
as a character witness. I don't know.

00:01:31.291 --> 00:01:32.659
But it's a really astounding,

00:01:32.659 --> 00:01:34.394
astounding bad moment

00:01:34.394 --> 00:01:35.929
in the history of this country.

00:01:35.929 --> 00:01:36.763
Why do you say that?

00:01:39.399 --> 00:01:40.066
Because we've got

00:01:40.066 --> 00:01:41.968
a completely politicized prosecution.

00:01:41.968 --> 00:01:43.503
You know, your last segment,

00:01:43.503 --> 00:01:44.170
you had folks

00:01:44.170 --> 00:01:44.938
that actually talked

00:01:44.938 --> 00:01:46.773
openly about CNN appearances

00:01:46.773 --> 00:01:48.041
by Alvin Bragg

00:01:48.041 --> 00:01:50.510
running for camp for office, saying,

00:01:50.510 --> 00:01:52.178
I will target Donald Trump.

00:01:52.178 --> 00:01:52.779
I mean,

00:01:52.846 --> 00:01:53.913
that is not something

00:01:53.913 --> 00:01:55.248
to gloss over lightly.

00:01:55.248 --> 00:01:56.716
That is an upside down

00:01:56.716 --> 00:01:58.518
world of criminal justice.

00:01:58.518 --> 00:01:59.853
Where we don't follow evidence,

00:01:59.853 --> 00:02:02.222
we don't act judiciously as prosecutors.

00:02:02.222 --> 00:02:04.357
And I was a prosecutor for 27 years.

00:02:04.624 --> 00:02:06.459
Okay. So I have some background on this.

00:02:06.459 --> 00:02:07.127
You've got people

00:02:07.127 --> 00:02:08.394
that are announced politically

00:02:08.394 --> 00:02:10.330
they're going to target an individual.

00:02:10.330 --> 00:02:12.065
That is not the rule of law.

00:02:12.065 --> 00:02:13.233
That is not what this country

00:02:13.233 --> 00:02:14.334
was built upon.

00:02:14.334 --> 00:02:16.102
And so when you talk about Donald Trump

00:02:16.102 --> 00:02:18.204
being angry, he should be mean.

00:02:18.271 --> 00:02:19.606
I'm amazed he's not,

00:02:19.606 --> 00:02:21.207
you know, more apoplectic.

00:02:21.207 --> 00:02:23.176
But he is right to be angry

00:02:23.176 --> 00:02:24.677
at political persecution,

00:02:24.677 --> 00:02:25.879
which is what this case is.

00:02:25.879 --> 00:02:26.746
Is he angry?

00:02:26.746 --> 00:02:27.614
Have you spoken to him?

00:02:27.614 --> 00:02:28.848
Since this indictment happened?

00:02:31.017 --> 00:02:31.751
No, I don't talk

00:02:31.751 --> 00:02:33.620
about that kind of stuff. Sorry, Kaitlyn.

00:02:33.620 --> 00:02:35.321
What's your sense of what happened?

00:02:35.321 --> 00:02:36.055
How about that?

00:02:36.055 --> 00:02:36.656
What's your sense

00:02:36.656 --> 00:02:40.193
of what happens between now and Tuesday?

00:02:41.294 --> 00:02:42.729
Well, look, you know, I'll tell you,

00:02:42.729 --> 00:02:44.531
the big picture is,

00:02:44.531 --> 00:02:45.665
you know, if you're representing him

00:02:45.665 --> 00:02:47.066
on the New York case,

00:02:47.066 --> 00:02:48.234
you've got a lot of stuff

00:02:48.234 --> 00:02:49.135
to be focusing on.

00:02:49.135 --> 00:02:49.936
But one of them

00:02:49.936 --> 00:02:51.638
is going to be pretrial motions.

00:02:51.638 --> 00:02:53.606
I know Ali, in the earlier segment

00:02:53.606 --> 00:02:54.274
talked about how

00:02:54.274 --> 00:02:55.775
that's a part of the process.

00:02:55.775 --> 00:02:56.109
You know,

00:02:56.109 --> 00:02:57.410
you don't usually win

00:02:57.410 --> 00:02:59.445
on a pretrial motions saying, hey,

00:02:59.445 --> 00:03:01.114
the government's got the worst witnesses

00:03:01.114 --> 00:03:01.714
imaginable.

00:03:01.714 --> 00:03:03.449
Even if that happens to be true,

00:03:03.449 --> 00:03:04.984
you win on legal issues.

00:03:04.984 --> 00:03:07.353
And this case is all about.

00:03:07.353 --> 00:03:08.755
It looks like from the outside

00:03:08.755 --> 00:03:10.857
right now, mental gymnastics

00:03:10.857 --> 00:03:11.691
that don't add up.

00:03:11.691 --> 00:03:13.326
I mean, legal gymnastics,

00:03:13.326 --> 00:03:14.327
they're going to fall apart.

00:03:14.327 --> 00:03:16.396
So I would think in very short order,

00:03:16.396 --> 00:03:17.830
you'll see a motion to dismiss

00:03:17.830 --> 00:03:18.698
or several motions

00:03:18.698 --> 00:03:19.599
to dismiss

00:03:19.599 --> 00:03:20.733
Talking about this

00:03:20.733 --> 00:03:22.468
kind of impossible theory

00:03:22.468 --> 00:03:24.370
of stacking a federal crime

00:03:24.370 --> 00:03:25.572
into a state misdemeanor

00:03:25.572 --> 00:03:27.273
statute of limitations issues

00:03:27.273 --> 00:03:28.508
and very importantly,

00:03:28.508 --> 00:03:29.976
the intent to defraud.

00:03:29.976 --> 00:03:30.710
That's an element

00:03:30.710 --> 00:03:33.046
of these false recordkeeping charges

00:03:33.046 --> 00:03:34.914
that's just not present here

00:03:34.914 --> 00:03:36.316
under even the most dreamy

00:03:36.316 --> 00:03:37.784
of Michael Cohen moments.

00:03:37.784 --> 00:03:38.885
It's not part of the case.

00:03:38.885 --> 00:03:40.453
So there's a lot to look at.

00:03:40.453 --> 00:03:41.921
I think there'll be pretrial motions

00:03:41.921 --> 00:03:43.690
that will be hugely important

00:03:43.690 --> 00:03:44.691
and well-founded

00:03:44.691 --> 00:03:46.359
to dismiss this travesty,

00:03:46.359 --> 00:03:48.094
those motions to dismiss that.

00:03:48.094 --> 00:03:48.928
You say you're expecting

00:03:48.928 --> 00:03:49.996
will those come before

00:03:49.996 --> 00:03:52.365
the indictment is unsealed on Tuesday,

00:03:52.365 --> 00:03:53.800
or what is your expectation there?

00:03:55.902 --> 00:03:57.570
I don't know about the exact timing.

00:03:57.570 --> 00:03:59.372
I think the practical problem is,

00:03:59.372 --> 00:03:59.572
you know,

00:03:59.572 --> 00:04:00.740
we don't even have a case number.

00:04:00.740 --> 00:04:01.874
Keep in mind, with Donald Trump,

00:04:01.874 --> 00:04:03.076
there are no rules.

00:04:03.076 --> 00:04:03.810
So, once again,

00:04:03.810 --> 00:04:05.945
we have sealed proceedings

00:04:05.945 --> 00:04:07.113
that have been leaked publicly

00:04:07.113 --> 00:04:08.448
that we're all talking about.

00:04:08.448 --> 00:04:08.715
I mean, it's

00:04:08.715 --> 00:04:10.383
just kind of an amazing breakdown

00:04:10.383 --> 00:04:12.418
of due process and fair play.

00:04:12.418 --> 00:04:13.753
So we don't even have a case number

00:04:13.753 --> 00:04:15.655
at this moment. But it'll be soon.

00:04:15.655 --> 00:04:16.789
I think this will be something

00:04:16.789 --> 00:04:18.324
you can expect in days or weeks.

00:04:18.324 --> 00:04:20.059
Not not weeks or months.

00:04:20.059 --> 00:04:20.426
Okay.

00:04:20.426 --> 00:04:22.428
So you say there will likely be a motion

00:04:22.428 --> 00:04:24.130
to dismiss this. That's important.

00:04:24.130 --> 00:04:25.398
You are representing Trump

00:04:25.398 --> 00:04:26.933
in the January six investigation

00:04:26.933 --> 00:04:28.001
in the classified documents

00:04:28.001 --> 00:04:28.668
investigation.

00:04:28.668 --> 00:04:29.669
There are several

00:04:29.669 --> 00:04:31.004
investigations now

00:04:31.004 --> 00:04:31.604
facing him,

00:04:31.604 --> 00:04:33.239
including with this indictment.

00:04:33.239 --> 00:04:34.874
How does the legal team manage

00:04:34.874 --> 00:04:36.542
all of these investigations at once?

00:04:39.012 --> 00:04:40.146
Well, we've got a good team.

00:04:40.146 --> 00:04:41.281
We've got a lot of different people

00:04:41.281 --> 00:04:43.049
with a lot of different backgrounds

00:04:43.049 --> 00:04:44.884
and experience.

00:04:44.884 --> 00:04:45.818
You know, I will say

00:04:45.818 --> 00:04:47.020
the one common thread

00:04:47.020 --> 00:04:48.154
that I'm seeing is somebody

00:04:48.154 --> 00:04:51.224
who was associated with DOJ for 17 years

00:04:51.391 --> 00:04:52.625
and watching what's happening

00:04:52.625 --> 00:04:53.960
unfolding in New York

00:04:53.960 --> 00:04:55.561
is prosecutorial overreach.

00:04:55.561 --> 00:04:56.362
You know, there's an ends

00:04:56.362 --> 00:04:58.598
justify the means mentality

00:04:58.598 --> 00:04:59.699
that is unlike anything

00:04:59.699 --> 00:05:01.734
I've ever seen in prosecutorial circles.

00:05:01.734 --> 00:05:03.803
You've got people like Letitia James

00:05:03.803 --> 00:05:04.904
now, Alvin Bragg

00:05:04.904 --> 00:05:06.706
announcing we will get him.

00:05:06.706 --> 00:05:08.007
You've got an attorney general

00:05:08.007 --> 00:05:09.842
the United States doing press conferences

00:05:09.842 --> 00:05:11.044
after a search warrant,

00:05:11.044 --> 00:05:13.146
which is completely unprecedented,

00:05:13.146 --> 00:05:15.148
unprecedented and unethical.

00:05:15.415 --> 00:05:16.983
And so what we do is, you know,

00:05:16.983 --> 00:05:17.684
we kind of shadow

00:05:17.684 --> 00:05:18.584
the investigations,

00:05:18.584 --> 00:05:20.219
figure out the actual facts

00:05:20.219 --> 00:05:23.056
and find ways to litigate, often

00:05:23.323 --> 00:05:24.223
under seal.

00:05:24.223 --> 00:05:26.025
Some of the issues that are just rolling

00:05:26.025 --> 00:05:27.393
through these over

00:05:27.393 --> 00:05:29.329
these heavy handed investigations

00:05:29.329 --> 00:05:30.129
into the president,

00:05:30.129 --> 00:05:31.898
you know, he's got plenty of resources

00:05:31.898 --> 00:05:33.166
to bear to fight back.

00:05:33.166 --> 00:05:34.133
You noted all the attorneys

00:05:34.133 --> 00:05:34.600
here on the team.

00:05:34.600 --> 00:05:37.303
How many how many exactly are there

00:05:37.303 --> 00:05:38.638
how many attorneys are there representing

00:05:38.638 --> 00:05:39.672
Trump at this time?

00:05:41.974 --> 00:05:43.076
Oh, I don't I don't

00:05:43.076 --> 00:05:44.377
have an exact number for you.

00:05:44.377 --> 00:05:46.346
So when the war

00:05:46.346 --> 00:05:47.146
when you talk about all

00:05:47.146 --> 00:05:48.147
and Bragg and Trump

00:05:48.147 --> 00:05:49.582
has continued to attack him,

00:05:49.582 --> 00:05:51.084
he faced criticism over the weekend

00:05:51.084 --> 00:05:52.218
after there was a link

00:05:52.218 --> 00:05:53.119
that he posted on Troop

00:05:53.119 --> 00:05:54.253
Social that a photo of Trump

00:05:54.253 --> 00:05:55.154
holding a baseball bat

00:05:55.154 --> 00:05:56.989
next to a picture of Alvin Bragg.

00:05:56.989 --> 00:05:59.359
Is it inappropriate for the

00:05:59.359 --> 00:06:01.361
for your client to post things like that,

00:06:01.361 --> 00:06:02.929
attacking the district attorney,

00:06:02.929 --> 00:06:03.963
calling him an animal,

00:06:03.963 --> 00:06:06.065
calling him a racist?

00:06:07.266 --> 00:06:08.835
Well, as I understand it,

00:06:08.835 --> 00:06:10.970
the meme that got retweeted

00:06:10.970 --> 00:06:12.638
didn't actually have the image

00:06:12.638 --> 00:06:14.574
until it showed up on true social.

00:06:14.574 --> 00:06:16.142
So he didn't actually know

00:06:16.142 --> 00:06:17.176
that there was this

00:06:17.176 --> 00:06:19.178
baseball bat image thing.

00:06:19.178 --> 00:06:21.381
It's unfortunate that that happened.

00:06:21.381 --> 00:06:22.749
And there's a lot of room

00:06:22.749 --> 00:06:24.684
for an emotional reaction from anybody.

00:06:24.684 --> 00:06:25.284
Any client

00:06:25.284 --> 00:06:27.353
I have would be angry at this point.

00:06:27.587 --> 00:06:29.489
But the general concern

00:06:29.489 --> 00:06:30.790
that President Trump has,

00:06:30.790 --> 00:06:32.558
and I think it's a very genuine one,

00:06:32.558 --> 00:06:34.927
is that this is not even just about him.

00:06:34.927 --> 00:06:36.429
Yes, he's being targeted

00:06:36.429 --> 00:06:37.997
for political persecution,

00:06:37.997 --> 00:06:39.732
but this is an attack on the fabric

00:06:39.732 --> 00:06:40.366
of our system,

00:06:40.366 --> 00:06:42.168
on the whole presumption

00:06:42.168 --> 00:06:44.003
of innocence, due process,

00:06:44.003 --> 00:06:45.138
prosecutorial ethics.

00:06:45.138 --> 00:06:46.839
I mean, all of this is in play

00:06:46.839 --> 00:06:48.808
under that category of rule of law.

00:06:48.808 --> 00:06:50.643
And I'm as frustrated as anyone

00:06:50.643 --> 00:06:53.146
to see this kind of change in a system

00:06:53.413 --> 00:06:54.080
that heretofore

00:06:54.080 --> 00:06:55.481
had been the best in the world.

00:06:55.481 --> 00:06:56.416
You're representing Trump

00:06:56.416 --> 00:06:58.451
on the classified documents matter.

00:06:58.451 --> 00:06:59.419
Did he still know

00:06:59.419 --> 00:07:00.386
that there were documents,

00:07:00.386 --> 00:07:01.788
still classified documents,

00:07:01.788 --> 00:07:03.256
still at Mar a Lago

00:07:03.256 --> 00:07:04.991
after a subpoena came

00:07:04.991 --> 00:07:06.292
to return those documents

00:07:09.328 --> 00:07:10.897
I'm not going to get into the facts

00:07:10.897 --> 00:07:12.465
of any investigation that's pending.

00:07:12.465 --> 00:07:13.666
What I can tell you is

00:07:13.666 --> 00:07:14.901
you can't say whether or not

00:07:14.901 --> 00:07:17.670
the United States is there

00:07:19.005 --> 00:07:20.640
Caitlin, do you really expect

00:07:20.640 --> 00:07:21.274
that we're going to have

00:07:21.274 --> 00:07:22.375
that kind of conversation?

00:07:22.375 --> 00:07:23.976
I think you know better.

00:07:23.976 --> 00:07:25.311
But the reality is

00:07:25.311 --> 00:07:27.180
the president has every right.

00:07:27.180 --> 00:07:28.815
We entrust presidents

00:07:28.815 --> 00:07:30.216
under the Constitution

00:07:30.216 --> 00:07:32.418
to know state secrets, to be familiar

00:07:32.418 --> 00:07:33.252
with these things,

00:07:33.252 --> 00:07:34.153
to even hold on

00:07:34.153 --> 00:07:35.655
to documents and determine

00:07:35.655 --> 00:07:37.290
which ones they're going to hold on to

00:07:37.290 --> 00:07:37.824
and which ones

00:07:37.824 --> 00:07:39.625
they're going to give to the archives.

00:07:39.625 --> 00:07:43.029
So criminalizing that process was absurd.

00:07:43.062 --> 00:07:43.663
That's nothing

00:07:43.663 --> 00:07:44.997
that's ever happened in history.

00:07:44.997 --> 00:07:46.065
You've got thousands

00:07:46.065 --> 00:07:47.567
of classified documents

00:07:47.567 --> 00:07:48.701
sitting in Chicago

00:07:48.701 --> 00:07:50.336
for the Obama Foundation.

00:07:50.336 --> 00:07:51.504
No similar treatment.

00:07:51.504 --> 00:07:52.271
And that's really

00:07:52.271 --> 00:07:54.240
what President Trump is fighting about.

00:07:54.240 --> 00:07:55.641
And that's what we're fighting about

00:07:55.641 --> 00:07:56.943
is the idea that somehow

00:07:56.943 --> 00:07:58.744
this whole criminal justice system

00:07:58.744 --> 00:08:00.947
can be turned on its head because of him.

00:08:00.947 --> 00:08:01.180
You know,

00:08:01.180 --> 00:08:03.182
one person gets differential treatment

00:08:03.182 --> 00:08:04.484
across the board,

00:08:04.484 --> 00:08:05.685
whether it's criminalizing

00:08:05.685 --> 00:08:07.453
a civil dispute about documents,

00:08:07.453 --> 00:08:09.055
whether it's ignoring

00:08:09.055 --> 00:08:10.923
peaceful words on January six

00:08:10.923 --> 00:08:11.924
or threading together

